  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find the composite functions $g(f(x))$ and $f(g(x))$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p43-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=4$, for all $x$, and $g(x)=7$, for all $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(f(x))=7$ and $f(g(x))=4$, for all $x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(f(x))&=g(4)=7\\\\f(g(x))&=f(7)=4\\end{align*}$$Both hold for all $x$ because both functions are constant.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x$, $g(x)$ any function.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(f(x))=g(x)$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(f(x))&=g(x)\\\\f(g(x))&=g(x)\\end{align*}$$The identity function leaves its input unchanged, so both composites equal $g$ on its domain.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      }
    ]
  },
